# Backend Testing

Stack: Jest + ts-jest. Shared helpers live in `@nestlancer/testing`.

## Layout
- Unit: `**/tests/unit/**/*.spec.ts`
- Integration: `**/tests/integration/**/*.spec.ts`
- Package e2e: `**/e2e/**/*e2e-spec.ts` with local `e2e/setup.ts` / `e2e/jest.e2e.config.ts`
- System: `tests/system/**/*.{smoke,e2e}.spec.ts` (live infra; sequential)

## Commands
- `pnpm test:unit` / `pnpm test:integration` / `pnpm test:e2e`
- `pnpm test:system:smoke` for health/smoke against running stack
- `pnpm test:cov` for coverage

## Required coverage when changing code
- Auth, payments, webhooks, admin impersonation, media uploads: unit + at least one integration or e2e path
- Controllers/DTOs: validation failure cases (400 envelope), authz denial (401/403)
- Services with Prisma: mock write/read clients; assert soft-delete and transaction boundaries
- Workers/outbox: idempotent consume + failure/DLQ behavior
- Do not rely on `forceExit` to hide leaked handles; clean up connections in `afterAll`

## Style
- Prefer `@nestlancer/testing` UUID mock and factory helpers
- Mirror source names: `foo.service.ts` → `foo.service.spec.ts`
- CI currently runs unit tests only — still write integration/e2e for risk paths locally before merge
